{
  "abstract": "Starting from the five polynomial reciprocal-product detectors of lihongmin, we identify the canonical profile at every residue level. Nonnegative periodization, zero mean, endpoint conditions, and the first $\\ell$ missing odd coefficients force degree at least $3\\ell+3$; at that degree the polynomial is unique up to positive scaling. The proof uses one rational Mellin numerator argument instead of separate finite rank calculations. We construct the entire algebraic family through a product of independent beta variables and prove that, after scaling the argument by $3\\sqrt{\\ell}/2$, the signed profiles converge locally uniformly to a Gaussian derivative. Their periodizations converge locally uniformly on positive scales to the classical positive Riemann theta derivative kernel, whose Mellin transform is the completed zeta function up to its conventional power of pi. We also compute the first correction to the limiting Mellin factor and give explicit positive end regions at every level. Exact rational Bernstein certificates extend global periodization positivity from five levels through level twelve, adding degrees 21 through 39. The supplementary standard-library verifier reconstructs these identities independently and checks an alternative beta-integral construction. The Gaussian limit yields eventual positivity on each compact scaling interval, but does not prove global positivity at every level. No new zeta zero-free region or bound for the signed arithmetic form is obtained; the corresponding RH criteria use the established Möbius-convolution mechanism.",
